# The tutorial library

The functions the lessons use to check your exercises and count your
progress. A lesson imports this document, on a hidden line at its top, and
binds its names as `tutorial`.

- `tutorial.check ok` shows "✓ Done" if `ok` is true, and "○ Not yet"
  otherwise, also when `ok` cannot be computed yet.
- `tutorial.progress lesson` counts the checks of an imported lesson: how
  many show "✓ Done", out of how many.
- `tutorial.tag code` writes a formula as an example, between its brackets,
  without running it.

<%
DONE = "✓ Done",
NOT_YET = "○ Not yet",

check = ok -> ok ? DONE ; NOT_YET,

# How many tags of an imported document showed `value`.
count = (value, doc) -> list.size [(list.enum doc.tags) => (t -> (t.value == value) ? 1)],

progress = doc -> (
    done = count (DONE, doc),
    total = done + count (NOT_YET, doc),
    (total == 0) ? "try it" ;
    (done == total) ? "✓ " + text.from done + " of " + text.from total ;
    text.from done + " of " + text.from total
),

# The brackets of a formula cannot be written as text in a document: they
# would start one. These produce them.
OPEN = "<" + "%",
CLOSE = "%" + ">",
tag = code -> "`" + OPEN + " " + code + " " + CLOSE + "`"
%>
